Third-party schemas this standard is checked against (no normative text is copied; their element names are data-model names):

- ISA-95 (IEC 62264) objects, fields and edge paths: MESA International B2MML (github.com/MESAInternational/B2MML-BatchML).
  "The Business To Manufacturing Markup Language (B2MML) is used courtesy of MESA International."
- ISA-88 (IEC 61512) objects, fields and edge paths (core 4.1.0, standard/profiles/batch/): MESA International BatchML 0701, same repository.
  "The Batch Markup Language (BatchML) is used courtesy of MESA International."
  "The Batch Markup Language (BatchML) is used courtesy of the World Batch Forum." (the statement BatchML-BatchInformation.xsd asks for)
